+# Skill Capability Tiers
+
+fetch-helper: Active (tool-augmented)
+tone-guide: Passive (knowledge-only)
+
+---
+
+## Evidence
+
+### fetch-helper — Active (tool-augmented)
+
+- **Files present:** `SKILL.md` + `scripts/update.sh`
+- **`SKILL.md` description:** *"Keeps the project's helper toolchain up to date."* — explicitly an action-oriented purpose.
+- **Instructions in `SKILL.md`:** directs the agent to run a shell script (`scripts/update.sh`), then invoke a binary (`helper --version`), and conditionally show error output — all imperative, side-effecting steps.
+- **`scripts/update.sh`:** a `curl -fsSL … | sh` pipeline that downloads and executes an external bootstrap script. This is a real system-level operation (network I/O + code execution).
+- **Conclusion:** the skill bundles executable infrastructure and instructs the agent to invoke it, placing it firmly in the **active / tool-augmented** tier.
+
+---
+
+### tone-guide — Passive (knowledge-only)
+
+- **Files present:** `SKILL.md` only — no scripts, no helper files, no external resources.
+- **`SKILL.md` description:** *"House style for release notes and changelog entries."* — purely informational purpose.
+- **Instructions in `SKILL.md`:** six prose style rules (word choice, bullet length, framing). Every rule constrains *how the agent writes*, not *what the agent does*. No tool calls, no commands, no network access, no file mutations are requested.
+- **Conclusion:** the skill is a static reference document that shapes language output only, placing it firmly in the **passive / knowledge-only** tier.
